+
+# Best AI Tools for Recruiters 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-recruiters-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best AI tools for recruiters 2026 is a curated list of open source GitHub projects recruiters can actually inspect, fork, and self-host. Instead of proprietary SaaS, this list focuses on recruiter-facing ATS platforms, resume parsers, candidate-matching tools, and recruiting agents that exist as public repositories and are useful for building a transparent hiring stack.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- [`srbhr/Resume-Matcher`](https://github.com/srbhr/Resume-Matcher) is the strongest open source option for resume-to-job matching and ATS-style keyword optimization.
+- [`xitanggg/open-resume`](https://github.com/xitanggg/open-resume) is the most polished open source resume toolkit in this space and pairs well with screening workflows.
+- [`opencats/OpenCATS`](https://github.com/opencats/OpenCATS) remains the best-known self-hosted ATS foundation for teams that want full control.
+- [`OmkarPathak/pyresparser`](https://github.com/OmkarPathak/pyresparser) is still one of the most practical OSS resume parsing libraries for recruiter workflows.
+- The recruiter-native open source AI ecosystem is still thin, so some categories below are explicitly marked as gaps and include experimental projects.
+
+## Why This List
+Most lists of the best AI tools for recruiters are dominated by closed SaaS products. That makes vendor lock-in, unclear scoring logic, and limited customization the default. This repository takes the opposite approach: every entry is a public GitHub repository, so recruiters, talent ops teams, and builders can inspect the code, verify licenses, and compose their own recruiting stack around parsing, matching, ranking, outreach, and applicant tracking.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Applicant Tracking Systems And Recruiting Platforms
+
+#### [OpenCATS](https://github.com/opencats/OpenCATS)
+> **Description:** OpenCATS is the longest-running open source ATS in this list and is built for managing recruiting pipelines, candidate records, submissions, interviews, and activity history in a self-hosted environment. Its README and docs focus on full-text search, resume ingestion, configurable workflows, and classic agency or in-house recruiting operations. It is not an LLM-native project, but it is still one of the most practical foundations for recruiters who want an auditable system they can extend with AI parsing or ranking. GitHub metadata: last commit date Jul 8, 2025, 659 stars, PHP, GPL-2.0.
+
